<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottokar I of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1155–<a href="/years/1230">1230</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Přemysl Ottokar I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ottokar I was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and from 1198 its king. Exploiting the rivalry between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-swabia">Philip of Swabia</a> and Otto IV for the German crown, he secured a hereditary royal title, confirmed by Frederick II in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-sicily">Golden Bull of Sicily</a> of 1212. His long reign strengthened the Přemyslid state and encouraged the founding of towns and German settlement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottokar-i-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="Ottokar I of Bohemia" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Packare · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OttocarusPrimus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
